      "excerpt": "         I2.9.1 To prevent local buckling in the web, the ratio of web height (hw) to net web thickness\n         (twn) of any framing member is not to exceed:\n\n         For flat bar sections:                     hw / twn ≤ 282 / (y)0.5\n\n         For bulb, tee and angle sections:          hw / twn ≤ 805 / (y)0.5\n\n              where hw = web height\n                    twn = net web thickness\n                    y = minimum upper yield stress of the material [N/mm2]\n",
